     <h1 class="title" title="Kufri Hill Station">Kufri</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/north-india-hill-stations/Kufri-hill-station.jpg" title="Kufri hill station" alt="Kufri hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Kufri" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Himachal Pradesh<br />
<b>Area:</b> 47sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Winter sports capital of Himachal Pradesh <br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2510m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 20&#176;C - 30&#176;C, Winter 10&#176;C - 10&#176;C .<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b>  April-June</p>
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Snow, mountains</p>
<p><b>Kufri</b> is located at an altitude of about 2500m ASL. It is 16 km on <b>NH 22</b> is this small town known for its <b>skiing in winter</b>. Once a Kufer or pond, Kufri has become an <b>exotic holiday destination</b>. There is also an aviary housing some <b>Himalayan mountain birds</b> like Monal, the <b>state bird of Himachal Pradesh</b>. During the summer can be a horse and yak riding on the green meadows. One can trek to the summit <b>Mahasu adventure</b>. Some stations have been raised about the Kufri <b>Kufri-Chail road</b> for those seeking is far from the hustle and bustle of Shimla.</p>
